{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And he shall no longer serve</b> — the labor of carrying on the shoulder, but he returns to locking the gates, to singing, and to loading the wagons — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 8:25). But in Sifrei (BeHa'alotkha 63) they said only that this teaches he returns to locking the gates and to the labor of the sons of Gershon. And so it appears, for if according to the Rav's words, why would they not appoint them at the age of twenty for singing and for locking the gates and for loading the wagons until they grew old? And why was their count from thirty to fifty except for the carrying alone? And furthermore, the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari, whose entire labor is valid for the elderly, why were they counted so? Rather, since their assignment for carrying the Ark was from thirty to fifty, they would not appoint them for singing — which is the principal labor of the Levites — except those fit for carrying, for all those appointed for singing are fit for all the labors. And since the sons of Kohath were counted from thirty to fifty even for singing, all of them were counted so, that the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari should not be fit for singing during those years while the sons of Kohath are disqualified from it. But for locking the gates or loading the wagons, all of them are fit. And furthermore it is written: \"From thirty years old and upward even to fifty years old, all who come to perform the labor of service and the labor of carrying in the Tent of Meeting\" (Numbers 4:47), and they interpreted in Ḥullin (24a): I might say this applies also in Shiloh and in the Eternal House? The verse teaches: \"to perform the labor of service and the labor of carrying\" — I spoke only of a time when the labor is on the shoulder. And \"the labor of service\" is the singing, as Rashi wrote above in the portion of Naso (4:47). If so, they were also disqualified for singing during the time when the labor is on the shoulder. And so in David's words it is stated: \"And the Levites were counted from thirty years old and upward\" (I Chronicles 23:3), and it is written: \"Of these, to oversee the work of the house of YHWH, twenty-four thousand, etc., and four thousand praising YHWH with the instruments which I made for praise\" (ibid. vv. 4–5), for until the House was built, when they had carrying on the shoulder, they would not appoint for singing except those fit for carrying. But David went back to counting them from twenty for the needs of the House once it was built, as was explained (at the end of the previous statement)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :register {:flags {0 ["the Eternal"]}}, :notes {0 "The Rav refers to Maimonides, here cited as the source of Rashi's view that retired Levites return to singing and loading wagons; the reference in Rashi is to Numbers 8:25."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:03:53.389275808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}